// endpoint_update_queue_bypass_mode.proto — UpdateQueueBypassMode. TOPBAR
// section. Take or release a workspace's queue bypass mode.
//
// THE MODE IS THE REPOSITORY'S, HELD BY ONE WORKSPACE. While a workspace holds
// it, the repository's merge queue is HARD-STOPPED (whatever it was running
// stops at once, and nothing advances), and the workspace lands each change on
// the main branch itself. Releasing it resumes the queue. A second workspace
// of the same repository cannot take the mode until the holder releases it.
//
// THE MODE SWITCHES THE WORKSPACE'S CONVERSATION. A workspace keeps two: its
// ordinary one, whose system prompt carries the merge-queue rules, and its
// bypass one, whose system prompt carries the bypass directive instead and
// whose session never loads the merge-queue skill. Taking the mode ends the
// ordinary session and resumes the bypass conversation (or starts it fresh,
// the first time); releasing it does the reverse. Neither conversation's cache
// is spent by the other, and the one not running is kept for the next switch.
//
// ONLY A PERSONAL ACCOUNT MAY HOLD IT: a work account's workspace is refused,
// and its topbar draws no chip at all.
//
// A SWITCH IS NOT AN INTERRUPT: it is refused while a turn is in flight, as
// every other session-level verb is.

